I believe `page.goto` works as expected here. What it does is it navigates the page to the specified URL and navigation is resetting the world along with all the JS state, as it is supposed to. No wonder none of the installed routers work. Non-anchor navigation is equivalent to going to a new URL via `about:blank`. In order to perform the navigation that router can handle, you should actually click on a router-aware link or you should know the mechanics that the framework uses to support routing. In most cases it'll be history API, so instead of `page.goto` you should do

```js
await page.evaluate(() => {
  window.history.pushState('', '', '/route-not-exsist-5b45f7cd193ecc56339c64428079706a');
});
```

It is saying "Perform SPA navigation to the new URL that history controller will handle".

For the second use case, it would be something like this:

```js
// Make navigation that router can handle using history API, not hard page.goto:
await page.evaluate(() => {
    window.history.pushState('', '', '/search?query=DOES_NOT_EXSISTS');
  });

await mount(BrowsePage);
```

Unfortunately, it looked like the first test passed but it wasn't.. Did some debugging and found out that `window.history.pushState()` doesn't trigger the Vue router. So this won't work:

```typescript
await page.evaluate(() => {
  // history.state is needed because of: https://router.vuejs.org/guide/migration/#usage-of-history-state
  window.history.pushState(history.state, '', '/route-not-exsist-5b45f7cd193ecc56339c64428079706a');
});
```

Created an [example application](https://sand4rt.github.io/playwright-component-testing-vue/) to illustrate this. Code can be viewed [here](https://github.com/sand4rt/playwright-component-testing-vue/blob/page.goto/src/components/Component.vue). See also the [failing tests](https://github.com/sand4rt/playwright-component-testing-vue/blob/page.goto/src/components/Component.test.ts).

Don't know yet if other routers allow URL changes trough `window.history.pushState` and if there is a workaround for that?
